🌲 prove.rack-refuses-an-undeclared-org
   ├─ an undeclared org, not this grove's own → ✋, no file
   │  ├─ GROVE_ORG=aether · org=nobody
   │  ├─ rc=1 · keyrack.yml written: no
   │  │     ✋ ConstraintError: org 'nobody' has no declared rack table, and is not this grove's own (GROVE_ORG='aether')
   │  │        ⇒ a grove reaches its own org only (rule.require.a-grove-reaches-its-own-org-only)
   │  │        fix: declare the org's envs in grove_provision_5_12_rack_declared, in 5.12.rack/_.sh
   │  └─ ✔
   │
   ├─ a declared org → writes org + its envs
   │  ├─ GROVE_ORG=aether · org=aether
   │  ├─ rc=0 · keyrack.yml written: yes
   │  │  yml: org: aether
   │  │  yml: env.camp:
   │  │  yml:   - AWS_PROFILE
   │  │  yml: env.test:
   │  │  yml:   - AWS_PROFILE
   │  │  yml: env.prep:
   │  │  yml:   - AWS_PROFILE
   │  │  yml: env.prod:
   │  │  yml:   - AWS_PROFILE
   │  └─ ✔
   │
   └─ this grove's own org, with no table → camp only
      ├─ GROVE_ORG=newco · org=newco
      ├─ rc=0 · keyrack.yml written: yes
      │  yml: org: newco
      │  yml: env.camp:
      │  yml:   - AWS_PROFILE
      └─ ✔

